{"kind":"request","text":"Fix the dap problems that the SeaweedFS evaluation of 2026-10-27 found under load on one celld node. Hugh asked for these fixes on 2026-10-27. The record is notes/implementation/2026-10-27-seaweedfs-local-bucket.md (head f67050898b519cd4a195c83449feb5ba92c35dbb, branch planner/seaweedfs-eval-20261027, section 7), with raw output in ~/play/artroom-evidence/2026-10-27-seaweedfs-local-bucket/. None of these were caused by the store. Decide for each whether it is a builder slice, a design question first, or a celld matter, and file accordingly.\n\n1. About 1,000 members per room. From about 1,000 members, `add-member` answers 503 \"guard-incomplete. Outcome unknown\", so the room can no longer add members. The range guard on the member handle scans at most `guardScan` (1,000, PROPOSED_BOUNDS in packages/contract/src/bounds.ts) items and returns \"guard-incomplete\" (packages/derive/src/guards.ts:105). A uniqueness check on one slot should not need a scan that grows with the room. Evidence: raw/mini-logs/sustained/ (7,818 guard-incomplete refusals as rooms passed about 1,000 members).\n\n2. Session cap. `REQUESTS_PER_KEY` = 64 per key and scope (packages/scope/src/sessions.ts:385) answers 429 to new sessions. The client then falls back to signed reads, which were refused or saw fewer entries; one `dap verify --all` reported a false \"incomplete\" this way, and 5,655 reads failed this way in the sustained run. Decide the cap and what the client does when it is reached.\n\n3. `dap verify --all` limits. (a) It stops at 64 scopes; on a room with 578 members it took 585 s to report \"the limit of 64 scopes was reached\" (raw/mini-logs/crash-c1/verify-all.json). Rooms now have an inbox per member, so 64 scopes is about 60 members. (b) Run from a room other than the register's first one, it cannot verify the register (register \"missing-dependency\", raw/mini-logs/verify-c2-final.json): the key may not read other rooms' directories once its last signature is no longer recent. (c) The same rule stops the same key creating another room after that window.\n\n4. Idle cost of resident scopes. With about 2,000 resident cells and no requests, celld used 2.25 cores; after each restart celld restored about 700 cells with no request. The cause is not isolated; it fits cells with armed alarms. Find whether dap arms alarms on idle scopes (archive wake, dispatcher retries, inbox deadlines) and whether it needs to. A celld issue if dap does not.\n\n5. For the self-hosting note's next draft (no code fix asked here): a celld shutdown on one node never seals (`shutdown_handoff_stalled`, node record \"draining\": true with no `log` object), so section 4.7's drain check needs a single-node case; and a timed rule on a cold cell fired 20.2 s late because celld's waker scans every 60 s.\n\n6. For the Git host choice note (request cc0bf648, no code fix asked here): the creation admission (apps/room/creation-admission.ts) admits a register install only when ARTIFACTS_CONFIG names the register, also off Cloudflare.","body":{"conditions":"Each of items 1 to 4 is fixed on main with a witness that reproduces the evaluation's case, or is answered by a planner assert that says why not or which celld issue owns it; items 5 and 6 are carried into the named notes.","target":"inherit","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}